        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "k7",
            "text": "I wanted the first card on the site to feel alive without asking anything of the visitor. No controls, no scroll hijacking: a quiet scene that happens to be there, and a different one next time you look.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "k8",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "k9",
            "text": "Writing one shader by hand is an evening. Writing thirteen is a project I would never have started. That gap is exactly where a machine collaborator earns its place.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "promptBlock",
        "_key": "ka",
        "label": "Prompt",
        "note": "Pass 1 of 4",
        "text": "A small, calm three.js scene for a 300 × 224 card. Soft and slow, no interaction. A heading sits on top, so tell me whether it needs light or dark text. It must dispose cleanly and never render above a capped pixel ratio."
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "kb",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "kc",
            "text": "The first answers were competent and forgettable. The interesting work started when I stopped describing scenes and started describing constraints.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
